  "output": "Template scaffolded: `report-template.html` (11.5 KB, fully offline, no JS). Here's the structure and why:\n\n## Document Outline\n\n```\nhtml lang=\"en\"\n├── head\n│   ├── meta charset / viewport / title\n│   └── <style>  ← all CSS inline, incl. @media print\n└── body\n    ├── header      → h1 + report metadata (dl.meta)\n    ├── nav         → optional linked TOC (delete if unwanted)\n    ├── main\n    │   ├── section#summary      → Executive Summary\n    │   ├── section#dashboard    → RAG tiles\n    │   ├── section#milestones   → milestone table\n    │   ├── section#progress     → accomplishments list\n    │   ├── section#upcoming     → next-period commitments\n    │   ├── section#risks        → risk/issue register table\n    │   ├── section#decisions    → sponsor asks table\n    │   ├── section#budget       → spend vs. plan table\n    │   ├── section#changes      → change-request log\n    │   └── section#appendix     → glossary + references\n    └── footer      → confidentiality + contact\n```\n\n## Element Choices (semantic, not decorative)\n\n| Content | Element | Why |\n|---|---|---|\n| Report metadata | `<dl>` | Label/value pairs are literally what a definition list is |\n| RAG ratings | `<data class=\"rag rag-red\" value=\"red\">` | Visible text + machine-readable value for future scraping |\n| Dates | `<time datetime=\"2026-10-15\">` | Sortable, parseable, locale-independent |\n| % complete | `<meter min=\"0\" max=\"100\">` | Native visual gauge; falls back to readable text |\n| All tabular data | `<table>` + `<caption>` + `th scope=\"col\"` | Correct semantics, accessible, and tables are what non-technical editors find easiest to edit |\n| Glossary | `<dl>` again | Same reasoning as metadata |\n| Sections | `<section>` + `<h2>`, exactly one `<h1>` | Clean heading outline that screen readers and TOC generators can traverse |\n\n## Editability Conventions\n\n- **`[BRACKETED TOKENS]`** mark every fill point, highlighted with a `.placeholder` style (yellow halo) that auto-disappears in print\n- `<!-- EDIT: ... -->` comments state the fill rule at each spot (e.g., \"3–5 sentences, verdict first\")\n- Flat nesting — content sits in plain text nodes, no deep wrapper soup; anyone can edit in any text editor\n- Modular sections: budget/changes/TOC can be deleted whole without breaking layout\n- RAG coloring is a one-class swap (`rag-green` → `rag-red`), no CSS knowledge needed\n\n## Print/A11y built in\n\n- `@media print` with `break-inside: avoid` on rows/tiles and `break-after: avoid` on headings — browser Print-to-PDF yields a clean A4/Letter document\n- `scope=\"col\"` headers, captions on every table, single `<h1>` — screen-reader friendly out of the box\n\nNext step is yours: hand me the project data (items 1–3 minimum from the inventory) and I'll turn this skeleton into a populated report.",
